  "full_source_findings": [
    {
      "declaration": "n04Coordinates_reference_canonicalLengthInverse_envelope",
      "findings": [
        "ReferenceJets is applied at spatial order zero and the genuine unit point (1/2,0).",
        "The canonicalLengthInverse atom is exactly the reciprocal K.right m-K.left m; no extra numerical length premise is substituted.",
        "The resulting B is chosen before every component and refers to the unchanged T.sample(K.cell m)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "declaration": "n04Coordinates_unitAtom_absolute_envelope",
      "findings": [
        "The one fixed spatial state loss is selected from CurrentJets clause 2 before any spatial order.",
        "The actual material sample theorem with beta=3/4 and exponent zero gives a single positive CH for H(sample)^3/4, uniformly over K.cell.",
        "Reference and difference envelopes are chosen at the same spatial order. B=max(B0,B1) and A=B0+B1*CH are chosen before states, atoms, components, points or derivative indices.",
        "Raising the E0 exponents uses only the explicit sample floor hfloor. IsMaterialData is not treated as implying E0>=1.",
        "The genuine mixed-derivative difference decomposition is applied with its actual smoothness clauses. The triangle inequality and the explicitly nonnegative extra product yield A*E0^B*(1+parameterGrading).",
        "The same K, T, sample, state lift and derivative loss are retained. The parameter SmoothDirections tower is not reconstructed or asserted by this lemma."
      ]
    },
    {
      "declaration": "n04Coordinates_inverse_affine_power_cost",
      "findings": [
        "For nonnegative c and E>=1, W=(1+B)*E^B is at least one; c^i<=W^i<=W^s when i<=s.",
        "The pinned natural-power and real-power APIs have the required direction, including Real.rpow_mul_natCast.",
        "The resulting factor (1+B)^s*E^(B*s) covers s=0 and introduces no state derivative loss."
      ]
    },
    {
      "declaration": "n04Coordinates_canonicalAtom_absolute_envelope",
      "findings": [
        "The actual canonical interval positivity supplies both the inverse-affine MapsTo property and nonnegativity of its radial scale.",
        "The existing inverse-affine mixed derivative formula gives precisely (K.right m-K.left m)^(-i), with no angular scale.",
        "The canonicalLengthInverse reference atom pays this factor using the actual sample. The envelope exponent becomes BL*s+B and the coefficient becomes (1+BL)^s*A.",
        "Only numerical material costs depend on s; the fixed loss selected from CurrentJets is unchanged.",
        "The full actual CanonicalGeometry.atom composed with n07aCanonicalUnitInversePoint is the target n07aCanonicalAtomField, not an independently chosen representative."
      ]
    },
    {
      "declaration": "n04Coordinates_sectorParameterOfState_grading",
      "findings": [
        "The actual sector parameter is the subtype of z.state-referenceState together with the original scalar parameter.",
        "The pair grading and subtype grading expand to stateGrading(s)(z.state-referenceState)+abs(z.parameter).",
        "No comparison constant, new low base or altered parameter neighborhood is introduced."
      ]
    },
    {
      "declaration": "n04Coordinates_sectorCanonicalJetBounds_of_reference_current",
      "findings": [
        "The same loss is retained and coefficientEnvelope_pack(4*A,B) is selected for each spatial order before every state and component.",
        "The actual state-to-sector map satisfies both the original neighborhood membership and the literal lift equality.",
        "The four literal atoms are potential, dividedA, dividedB and dividedC. The positive-piece Bool condition is preserved; on negative pieces only the potential is required.",
        "The four corrected comp_def rewrites expose the actual unit-point/inverse-point cancellation as a function equality under mixedDerivative.",
        "The sum of the four bounds is at most 4*V. The explicit E0 floor justifies coefficient packing, and the exact grading identity gives the frozen SectorCanonicalJetBounds.",
        "The conclusion includes spatial order zero, keeps the original base and epsilon, and assumes actual ReferenceJets and CurrentJets rather than a final estimate surrogate."
      ]
    }
  ],
